# Show the variants

A concept or a question is not complete when the lab shows only the winner. The user must see the difference and the tradeoff, then choose.

Show each important variant from the comparison table when a small demo can do it. Put the variants side by side in the UI. Show the request, the store that was used, and the result.

Name the interview default in the page and in the README. The other variants stay available so the user can compare them.

A notes-only topic (for example numbers to know) uses the comparison table as the breadth. Say that in the README.

Record the choice and the reason in the session notes. Do not delete a variant from the lab because the interview default is a different option.
